        "text": "Let's recall what prime numbers and even numbers are.\n\nA prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself. The smallest prime number is 2. An even number is any integer that is divisible by 2, so numbers like 2, 4, 6, 8, etc."
