        "text": "On the other hand, the right-hand side is (A - C) ∪ (B - C). Let's unpack that. An element x is in (A - C) if x is in A and x is not in C. Similarly, x is in (B - C) if x is in B and x is not in C. So, the union of these two sets would include all elements that are in A but not in C, or in B but not in C, or in both."
