        "text": "Okay, so I've come across this interesting puzzle about a prisoner who needs to take pills. Let me try to figure out how he can survive. The setup is that there are two identical-looking pills on the table: one is a harmless vitamin, and the other is deadly poison. The prisoner must take exactly one pill today and one pill tomorrow to survive. If he takes both vitamins or both poisons, he dies. He can't test the pills by any means—no taste, smell, or appearance. Also, he has no way to tell the pills apart, so he can't just look at them or distinguish them.\n\nBut here's the twist: the jailer knocked over the pill container, and both pills fell onto the table mixed with two new identical pills. So now there are four pills on the table: two vitamins and two poisons. The challenge is to figure out a way for the prisoner to guarantee survival."
