        "text": "Let me denote:\n\n- P(D) = probability of having the disease = 1/10,000 = 0.0001.\n\n- P(~D) = probability of not having the disease = 1 - 0.0001 = 0.9999.\n\n- P(Positive | D) = probability of testing positive given they have the disease = 0.99.\n\n- P(Negative | D) = probability of testing negative given they have the disease = 0.01.\n\n- P(Positive | ~D) = probability of testing positive given they don't have the disease = 0.01.\n\n- P(Negative | ~D) = probability of testing negative given they don't have the disease = 0.99.\n\nWe need to find P(D | Positive), the probability that someone has the disease given that they tested positive."
